/* The header for this test is at the BOTTOM of this file, below the script.
   It is there because a constant inside a leading comment can swallow the
   rest of the file in the engine - see RMSTEST_56 and the directory README.
   Nothing below the script can do any harm. */

<PLAYER_SETUP>
  random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
  base_terrain GRASS

  create_player_lands
  {
    terrain_type GRASS
    land_percent 10
  }

<ELEVATION_GENERATION>


<TERRAIN_GENERATION>

  create_terrain BOGLAND
  {
    base_terrain GRASS
    land_percent 30
    number_of_clumps 4
  }

<OBJECTS_GENERATION>


<CONNECTION_GENERATION>


/*
================================================================================
RMSTEST_81a - which terrain does BOGLAND paint now that Update 185872 made it
map type 123 in random_map.def? No include in this arm.
Feeds: RMS0316 (src/parser/validate.ts), and DE's own Murkwood.rms line 1095,
which writes create_terrain BOGLAND after including constants.inc.
Paired with RMSTEST_81b, whose only difference is the include line.
================================================================================

THE QUESTION
random_map.def (always loaded first) now says BOGLAND 123. constants.inc says
BOGLAND 101 (Swamp, Bogland). This arm has no include, so the only definition
in play is random_map.def's.

PREDICTION
About 30% of the map is terrain 123 (Grass, Flowers 2). No terrain 101 at all.

WHAT WOULD REFUTE IT
Any terrain 101. Or no painted clumps at all, which would mean BOGLAND does not
resolve as a terrain id here, a third reading nobody has proposed.

READ
Default probe histogram. Count tiles of 101 and of 123. By eye, bog is brown
swamp and 123 is green grass with flowers.
================================================================================
*/
